{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791600686,"nonce":"UYIXMo34txaMH4dMTxlZ5c9iQXI=","message":"Decision: the cross-site guard is a middleware on POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE for the whole console: a request carrying Origin or Sec-Fetch-Site must have a loopback Host and be same-origin, else 403; requests with neither header (curl, CLI, tests) pass; console --allow-remote drops only the loopback Host rule. Reason: browsers always send Origin on POST, so this blocks form auto-submit, no-cors fetch and DNS rebinding without breaking non-browser clients.","files":null}]}